    - taint_flow  # 08d0
    isbefore: []  # 08d0
    duplicate_of: []  # 08d0
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 08d0
    pr_ref:  # 08d0
    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-16 (round 4).**\n\n**Symptom.** Hypergumbo's own repo has a TypeScript WebSocket client connecting to a Python WebSocket handler within the repo, but the cross-language linker doesn't produce an edge between them.\n\n- Client: `packages/htrac-frontend/src/ws-client.ts` opens a WebSocket at `${proto}//${location.host}/ws`\n- Handler: `packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/serve.py:215` serves the `/ws` route (visible in `hypergumbo routes` output)\n- Cross-language edges connecting them in the behavior map: **0**\n\nTotal cross-language edges across the entire repo: 34. Breakdown:\n\n| src → dst | type | origin | count |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| python → toml | depends_on_manifest | dependency-linker-v1 | 26 |\n| typescript → javascript | uses | enclosure-linker-v1 | 7 |\n| html → javascript | script_src | html-pattern-v1 | 1 |\n\nNo python ↔ typescript pairs.\n\n**Why this matters.** The `websocket-linker-v1` produces 23 edges total. They are all within-language (e.g., Python handler ↔ Python message-publish sites, TS client ↔ TS topic-subscribe sites). The TS-frontend-to-Python-backend pairing — a textbook polyglot-app scenario — is the exact case the WebSocket Bridge linker should cover.\n\n**Hypotheses to verify.**\n\n1. **The WS URL is dynamic.** `${proto}//${location.host}/ws` is template-string-built at runtime. The linker's TS-side URL extractor may not normalize `${location.host}/ws` → `/ws`, so the path component never reaches the matcher.\n2. **The linker is single-language by design.** `websocket-linker-v1`'s probe may only walk a single-language symbol scope. If so, it's a Protocol-subcategory linker missing a Bridge-subcategory sibling per ADR-0003-ext.\n3. **The htrac-frontend package isn't analyzed by the WebSocket linker.** The package may not declare a manifest the linker recognizes; or the linker probes only Python WS frameworks (FastAPI/Starlette/Django Channels).\n4. **The path normalization differs.** Server registers `/ws`; client connects to `/ws` literally. Both should match if URL strings were extracted.\n\n**Expected behavior.** When (a) a client-side WS open call extracts a path component and (b) a server-side WS route declaration registers the same path (or a parameterized template that subsumes it), the Bridge linker should emit a `protocol_ws` / `websocket_route` / `uses` edge from the TS call site to the Python handler symbol. The exact edge type should follow the convention used by the HTTP route linker for client-server pairings (likely `routes_to` or `dispatches_to` with `meta.protocol=ws`).\n\n**Scope check.** Are other cross-language pairings also missing in this repo?\n\n| Pairing | Evidence in source | Edges? |\n|---|---|---|\n| TS `fetch('/api/...')` → Python handler | None — htrac-frontend only uses WS, not HTTP | n/a |\n| Python `subprocess.run(['gitleaks', ...])` → gitleaks (external binary) | yes (gitleaks.py:275) | Tracked by IO boundary, not cross-lang |\n| Python `subprocess.run(['pip', ...])` → external pip | yes | Same as above |\n\nOnly the TS↔Python WS pairing is missing. So this is a specific gap in the WebSocket linker, not a wholesale cross-language failure.\n\n**Recommended approach.**\n\n1. **Investigate root cause first** — read `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/websocket.py` (or the equivalent module) and determine which of the hypotheses (1)-(4) actually applies. The fix scope (1-line URL normalization vs. new Bridge-subcategory sibling) depends on this.\n2. **Add a regression test** — `packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_websocket_*.py` should grow a fixture with a TS client + Python handler at the same path, asserting an edge is emitted.\n3. **Self-analysis re-verification** — after the fix, count cross-language edges in `hg-self-analysis.json` and confirm the htrac-frontend ↔ serve.py edge appears.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n\n- `packages/htrac-frontend/src/ws-client.ts` (line referencing `${proto}//${location.host}/ws`)\n- `packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/serve.py:215` (WS handler)\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/websocket.py` (presumed location of the linker)\n- `docs/adr/0003-linker-subcategory-restoration.md` (Protocol vs Bridge subcategory distinction)\n- `docs/LINKERS.md` (linker catalog; check whether WS bridge is documented)\n\n**Notebook reference.** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_05162026_0438.md` Round 4 section."  # 08d0
    fields: {}  # 08d0
